# 7. Requirement 3: the benchmark service (benchmark/), the API behind the website's Performance page.
#    It runs the Task 3 k6 workloads from api-tests/task3 and keeps their results. Admin only.
#
# Start it with the benchmark project and seed it once (see api-tests/task3/README.md):
#   docker compose -p onlineshop-bench --profile benchmark up -d --build
#   node seed/benchmark-all.mjs 200000
#
# VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request. This file logs in once.
# Put the benchmark customer's password (printed by the seeder) in api-tests/.env as BENCHMARK_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@bench = http://localhost:8090/benchmark-api/v1
@adminEmail = {{$dotenv ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@adminPassword = {{$dotenv ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@customerPassword = {{$dotenv BENCHMARK_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD}}


###############################################################################
# Open: what the service is and what it can do
###############################################################################

### The API describes itself → 200 with every route
GET {{bench}}

### Health and k6 version → 200 { "status": "ok", "k6": "k6 v2.3.0 …" }
GET {{bench}}/health

### The five workloads and the fixtures they expect → 200
GET {{bench}}/cases


###############################################################################
# Auth: the shop's own admin token, checked by the shop API
###############################################################################

### Without a token → 401 Problem Details
GET {{bench}}/results

### Login admin (shop API) → 200
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### A made-up token → 401 "Your session is not valid." (a real customer token gets 403 "Admins only.")
GET {{bench}}/results
Authorization: Bearer not.a.valid-token


###############################################################################
# Before a run: is the data right?
###############################################################################

### Log in the benchmark customer (needed for orders-customer) → 200. The password is in the body, never in a URL.
POST {{bench}}/customer-session
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### Preflight: 200,000 orders, 4,000 for the customer, stock 100, ETag or not → 200 with "cases": { …: { "ready": true } }
GET {{bench}}/preflight
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}


###############################################################################
# Runs
###############################################################################

### Bad input → 400 with "field": "label"
POST {{bench}}/runs
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "not a label!",
  "cases": ["orders-first"]
}

### Start a quick run of one workload → 202 with a Location header. Use a new label each time:
### a saved result is never overwritten (the same label again → 409).
# @name startRun
POST {{bench}}/runs
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "try-{{$timestamp}}",
  "profile": "quick",
  "cases": ["product-hot"]
}

### Starting another one while it runs → 409 "A run is already going."
POST {{bench}}/runs
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "second-{{$timestamp}}",
  "profile": "quick",
  "cases": ["orders-first"]
}

### Follow it (send again every few seconds): "live" has the per-second p50/p95 while it runs → 200
GET {{bench}}/runs/{{startRun.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Cancel it → 202 (or 409 once it has finished)
POST {{bench}}/runs/{{startRun.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The run history, newest first → 200
GET {{bench}}/runs
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}


###############################################################################
# Results: the same files as the CLI (task3-results/<label>/<case>.json)
###############################################################################

### Every saved result, by label → 200
GET {{bench}}/results
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Compare "before" with the other labels: p50/p95/p99 reductions, same rules as report.mjs → 200
GET {{bench}}/compare?baseline=before
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Compare chosen labels only → 200
GET {{bench}}/compare?baseline=before&labels=after-index,after-redis
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}


###############################################################################
# Proofs: faster must not mean stale (api-tests/task3/verify.mjs)
###############################################################################

### Proof history → 200
GET {{bench}}/proofs
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ETag + stock edit → 200 with "passed": true once ETags exist ("passed": false, "no ETag yet" before)
POST {{bench}}/proofs/etag-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Read-after-write without confirming → 400: it places a real order and changes the fixtures
POST {{bench}}/proofs/read-after-write
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Read-after-write, confirmed (run it after your last timed run) → 200 with "passed": true
POST {{bench}}/proofs/read-after-write
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptDatasetChange": true
}
